.TH BRKAS 1 "2026-11-13" "brkas" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brkas \- build Buildroot projects described in YAML files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brkas
[\fB\-\-work\-dir\fR \fIdir\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIproject\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brkas
reads a project file, which names a Buildroot tree, br2-external trees, a
defconfig and configuration changes. It checks out the sources, configures
Buildroot and builds the project.
.PP
\fIproject\fR is a project file, or several joined with a colon
(\fIa.yml\fR:\fIb.yml\fR); later files override earlier ones.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-work\-dir " dir"
Work directory, see FILES. Default: \fB$BRKAS_WORK_DIR\fR, else the current
directory.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR init " [\fIdirectory\fR]"
Create a demo project in \fIdirectory\fR (default: the current one):
\fBdemo.yml\fR, \fBREADME.md\fR and \fB.gitignore\fR. Run \fBgit init \-b
main\fR unless the directory is in a git repository. Never overwrite a file.
.TP
.BI checkout " project"
Check out the sources and configure the output directory.
.TP
.BI build " project " "\fR[\fItarget\fR...]"
Check out, configure and run make. The default targets come from
\fBbuild.targets\fR, else \fBall\fR.
.TP
.BI shell " project"
Run bash in the output directory, with \fBhost/environment-setup\fR sourced.
Enable \fBBR2_PACKAGE_HOST_ENVIRONMENT_SETUP\fR, and run \fBmake sdk\fR
when the SDK is missing or the configuration changed. The output of
\fBmake sdk\fR goes to \fBbrkas\-sdk.log\fR in the output directory.
.TP
.BI menuconfig " project"
.TQ
.BI xconfig " project"
Run the Buildroot configuration tool, then print the options that changed.
xconfig needs Qt 5.
.TP
.BI dump " project"
Print the merged project.
.TP
.BI lock " project"
Write the lock file of the project, see FILES.
.TP
.BI for\-all\-repos " project command"
Run the shell \fIcommand\fR in each repository, with \fBBRKAS_REPO_NAME\fR,
\fBBRKAS_REPO_DIR\fR, \fBBRKAS_REPO_URL\fR and \fBBRKAS_REPO_COMMIT\fR set.
.TP
.BR clean " [\fIproject\fR]"
Remove the output directory of \fIproject\fR. Without \fIproject\fR,
\fB\-\-all\fR is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
These options apply to every command that takes a project, except
\fBclean\fR and \fBinit\fR:
.TP
.B \-\-update
Fetch the repositories, to follow their branches. \fBlock \-\-update\fR also
ignores the existing lock file.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Discard local changes in the repositories.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " dir"
Output directory. Default: \fBbuild/\fR\fIname\fR in the work directory.
.PP
Options of single commands:
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
\fBcheckout\fR: only check out the sources.
.TP
.B \-\-reconfigure
\fBcheckout\fR, \fBbuild\fR: configure again from scratch.
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-command " command"
\fBshell\fR: run \fIcommand\fR instead of an interactive shell.
.TP
.BI \-\-save " fragment"
\fBmenuconfig\fR, \fBxconfig\fR: write the changed options to \fIfragment\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-lock
\fBdump\fR: print what \fBlock\fR would write.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-checkout
\fBdump\fR, \fBfor\-all\-repos\fR: use the repositories as they are.
.TP
.B \-\-all
\fBclean\fR: also remove the repositories that brkas checked out. Without a
project: remove \fBbuild/\fR, \fBdownloads/\fR and every repository brkas
checked out in the work directory.
.TP
.B \-\-cache
\fBclean\fR: remove only the download cache of the project; with
\fB\-\-all\fR, the cache too.
.TP
.B \-\-force
\fBclean\fR: remove repositories even when they hold changed or new files,
or commits that are on no remote. Without it, \fBclean\fR removes nothing in
that case.
.SH PROJECT FILE
A YAML mapping with these keys:
.TP
.B header
\fBversion\fR: 1. \fBincludes\fR: files to read first, as paths or
\fB{repo:, file:}\fR.
.TP
.B buildroot
One of: \fBurl\fR and \fBrefspec\fR (git); \fBrelease\fR or \fBtarball\fR,
with \fBsha256\fR; \fBdir\fR (an existing directory). \fBpatches\fR: patch
files or directories, applied after the checkout.
.TP
.B externals
br2-external trees by name, with the keys of \fBbuildroot\fR, plus
\fBpath\fR, the external inside the repository.
.TP
.B defconfig
A defconfig name, a file path, or \fB{repo:, file:}\fR.
.TP
.B fragments
Configuration fragments by name, applied in order.
.TP
.B config
Single \fBBR2_\fR options, applied last.
.TP
.B build
\fBdir\fR, \fBname\fR, \fBtargets\fR, \fBdl_dir\fR.
.TP
.B env
Environment variables for make.
.TP
.B container
Defaults for \fBbrkas\-container\fR(1): \fBimage\fR, \fBengine\fR,
\fBoptions\fR.
.PP
Mappings merge key by key, other values replace earlier ones, and \fBnull\fR
removes a key. Paths are relative to the file that contains them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I work directory
\fBbuildroot/\fR, one directory per external cloned from git,
\fBbuild/\fR\fIname\fR\fB/\fR, \fBdownloads/\fR. Each directory brkas
creates inside a git repository is added to its \fB.git/info/exclude\fR.
.TP
.IB project .lock.yml
Next to the project file; next to the last file of a chain. The commit of
each git repository and the SHA-256 of each tarball. Read automatically.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BRKAS_WORK_DIR
Default work directory.
.TP
.B BR2_DL_DIR
Download cache, when the project sets no \fBbuild.dl_dir\fR.
.TP
.BR BRKAS_OUTPUT ", " BRKAS_BUILDROOT
Set in \fBshell\fR: the output directory and the Buildroot tree.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 130 when interrupted. \fBshell\fR exits with the
status of the shell; \fBfor\-all\-repos\fR is nonzero when a command failed.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
brkas init myproject
cd myproject
brkas build demo.yml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brkas\-container (1)
